{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["And they shall put it on the pole — R. Yosef Kara erred in this. Since it is not written as one would expect: במוט בשנים — and he wanted to say that the entire pole was beneath the vessels, based on what is written: על. I replied: for the poles were at the sides of the vessels, in the manner of any load where one inserts the poles into the rings on the sides of the vessels, as written in the section on the Tabernacle. But with the expression ונתנו it is fitting to say על המוט, while with the language of carrying it says במוט, as written: וישאוהו במוט. And so ונשא בם את השלחן, as written: בכתף ישאו — you have no carrying except on the shoulder, that is to say: by this means they carry this."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:49:45.063038817Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}